{
  "meta": {
    "name": "Forte Advice Design System",
    "version": "0.7.0",
    "updated": "2026-09-05"
  },
  "brand": {
    "icons": {
      "library": "phosphor",
      "defaultWeight": "regular",
      "weights": ["thin", "light", "regular", "bold", "fill", "duotone"],
      "defaultSizes": [16, 20, 24, 28],
      "buttonSize": 14
    },
    "typography": {
      "fontFamily": {
        "sans": "Geist",
        "mono": "Geist Mono",
        "powerpoint": "Aptos",
        "powerpointHeading": "Aptos Display"
      },
      "fontWeight": {
        "regular": 400,
        "medium": 500,
        "semibold": 600,
        "bold": 700
      },
      "scale": {
        "h1": { "fontSize": "2.25rem", "lineHeight": "2.5rem", "fontWeight": 700, "tailwind": "text-4xl font-bold" },
        "h2": { "fontSize": "1.875rem", "lineHeight": "2.25rem", "fontWeight": 600, "tailwind": "text-3xl font-semibold" },
        "h3": { "fontSize": "1.5rem", "lineHeight": "2rem", "fontWeight": 600, "tailwind": "text-2xl font-semibold" },
        "h4": { "fontSize": "1.25rem", "lineHeight": "1.75rem", "fontWeight": 600, "tailwind": "text-xl font-semibold" },
        "body": { "fontSize": "1rem", "lineHeight": "1.5rem", "fontWeight": 400, "tailwind": "text-base" },
        "bodySmall": { "fontSize": "0.875rem", "lineHeight": "1.25rem", "fontWeight": 400, "tailwind": "text-sm" },
        "caption": { "fontSize": "0.75rem", "lineHeight": "1rem", "fontWeight": 500, "tailwind": "text-xs font-medium" },
        "code": { "fontSize": "0.875rem", "lineHeight": "1.25rem", "fontWeight": 400, "tailwind": "text-sm font-mono" }
      },
      "notes": {
        "powerpoint": "Aptos and Aptos Display are used in PowerPoint templates instead of Geist, since Aptos ships with Microsoft 365 and works without per-machine font installation. For all web/digital products, use Geist."
      }
    }
  },
  "radius": {
    "none": "0",
    "input": "0.5rem",
    "card": "0.75rem",
    "pill": "9999px",
    "shadcnBase": "0.625rem"
  },
  "motion": {
    "duration": "300ms",
    "easing": "ease-out"
  },
  "components": {
    "button": {
      "height": "44px",
      "paddingX": "24px",
      "radius": "9999px",
      "iconSize": "14px",
      "iconCircleSize": "44px",
      "iconCircleOverlap": "-12px",
      "textOnlyIconGap": "8px"
    },
    "card": {
      "padding": "24px",
      "radius": "0.75rem"
    },
    "input": {
      "paddingX": "16px",
      "paddingY": "10px",
      "radius": "0.5rem"
    },
    "focusRing": {
      "width": "2px",
      "offset": "2px"
    }
  },
  "notes": {
    "spacing": "There is deliberately no bespoke spacing scale. Layout spacing follows Tailwind's default 4px scale (gap-2, px-6, p-6 and friends), which is what every recipe in design.md is written against; a parallel Forte scale would only be able to drift from it. What IS a Forte decision — the fixed dimensions of buttons, cards, inputs and the focus ring — lives in `components` above.",
    "radius": "radius.shadcnBase is shadcn/ui's own --radius, from which it derives its sm/md/lg/xl steps. It is separate from the semantic entries because it sizes shadcn's components, not Forte's."
  },
  "colors": {
    "notes": {
      "colorScheme": "Each mode declares colorScheme so the generated CSS can emit the color-scheme property. Without it, native scrollbars, selects and date pickers stay light on a dark surface.",
      "errorForeground": "Text/icon colour for content sitting on state.error (shadcn --destructive-foreground). It is cream rather than the per-mode text.inverted, because text.inverted is dark plum in the dark modes and would be unreadable on the error red.",
      "focus": "The focus ring colour is mode-dependent and lives in each entry of colors.modes, surfaced as --focus / ring-focus. There is deliberately no colors.state.focus: a single global value would contradict the per-mode ones. Every value clears WCAG SC 1.4.11 (3:1) against both of its mode's surfaces, which validate.js enforces. Each is a step from the mode's own tone scale: highlight is kept where it clears the bar (Burgendy/Cream) but cannot be used on cream or ash grey, where it only reaches 2.5:1 and 2.1:1."
    },
